l,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2014-10-17T01:58:46Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/comments/59459918","html_url":"https://github.com/rails/rails/issues/17294#issuecomment-59459918","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/17294","id":59459918,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU5NDU5OTE4","user":{"login":"chancancode","id":55829,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1ODI5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55829?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode","html_url":"https://github.com/chancancode","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2014-10-17T02:52:04Z","updated_at":"2014-10-17T02:56:44Z","body":"@schneems thanks for looking into this :smile:\n\nActually, checking again, `only_path` simply doesn't work with `*_url` anymore – the option is just ignored entirely when used with a `*_url` helper. Since it's not documented (or I just don't know where they would be documented), I'm okay with that, but...\n1. The error should be updated to remove the reference to `only_path`, because that doesn't work anymore.\n2. At least in 4.2, we should probably check for using `only_path` option with `*_url` and raise an error if it's present since that was recommended before. Likewise, `*_path` with `only_path` should also raise. I _know_ for a fact that these are being used today so having them just suddenly behave differently would break apps out there. In fact, something like this should probably go through a deprecation cycle first? Not knowing about this until your app tries to render an infrequently-visited page and blow up doesn't seem too great... (@tenderlove wdyt?)\n3. We are back to square one on the `_path` deprecation...\n\nOn the third point, while I agree that \"by default we should generate full URLs\", and I'd be okay with \"making it hard to generate paths so people don't shoot themselves in the foot\", we should probably still provide an escape valve for those \"I _really_ want a path scenarios\". I agree with @fxn that making it impossible to generate a path seems too strong.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/comments/59459918/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"chancancode","id":55829,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1ODI5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55829?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode","html_url":"https://github.com/chancancode","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chancancode/receiv